  "kind": "zone3",
  "name": "Zone 3 · shaded natural garden",
  "notes": "Shaded natural garden (Zone 3, phase 1–2). A low-care garden of plants that thrive in mixed semi-forest, north and north-west of the house along the trail.\nLight and fire: lop the large heavy-canopy eucalypt in this zone to open light and cut fuel near the house (check council vegetation rules and Land for Wildlife advice first; use an arborist). Thinning here also lights up the terraced fruit forest next door.\nPlants that look after themselves under part shade: native ginger, native yam, native grape, Molucca raspberry, warrigal greens, gotu kola, sweet leaf (katuk, cooked), Okinawa and Brazilian spinach, Queensland arrowroot, ginger and turmeric, comfrey, lomandra, dianella, native violet, midyim.\nBrighter patches after lopping: bananas (green, moist, low fire risk), finger lime, Davidson's plum, lilly pilly.\nWater: rain plus mulch; a drip line from the tank in the first dry spring.\nPlan: Bright Tree planting calendar and phasing (Oct 2026).",
